    <Placemark>
      <name>Horbat Radum (חורבת רדום)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Horbat Radum (חורבת רדום)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.35 (Pages 170, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Two depressions, approximately 2m in diameter, were found outside the northern wall of this late Iron Age II fortress. These are identified as likely blocked cisterns that served the fortification. Cisterns or pools were found at Radum, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
