    <Placemark>
      <name>Ibleam (Khirbet Bel&apos;ameh) (יבלעם (ח&apos;רבת בלעמה))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Ibleam (Khirbet Bel&apos;ameh) (יבלעם (ח&apos;רבת בלעמה))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Tunnel Shaft</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Samaria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.4, Summary (186) (Pages 127, 128, 186, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A rock-cut tunnel, approximately 100m long with steps, leading from the Bir Sinjil spring into the ancient tel, characteristic of Iron Age II water systems. Listed as one of 17 sites in Iron Age II Israel with a monumental water system, likely involving a tunnel or shaft to access groundwater within the fortified city. A water system, cut to a spring or groundwater within the fortified city, was found at Ibleam, dating to the Iron Age II.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Ibleam (Khirbet Bel&apos;ameh)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>יבלעם (ח&apos;רבת בלעמה)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Era"><value>09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Water Tunnel Shaft</value></Data>
        <Data name="Region"><value>Samaria</value></Data>
        <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
