    <Placemark>
      <name>Kadesh Barnea (Ein el-Gudeirat) (קדש ברנע (עין אל-קודייראת))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Kadesh Barnea (Ein el-Gudeirat) (קדש ברנע (עין אל-קודייראת))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.18, Summary (186) (Pages 159, 186, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A water system in the Middle Fortress (8th-7th centuries BCE) consisting of a stone-built, plastered reservoir (approx. 140 cubic meters) with 25 steps leading to its bottom, fed by a plastered channel from the main spring, Ein Qudeirat. Listed as one of 17 sites in Iron Age II Israel with a monumental water system, likely involving a tunnel or shaft to access groundwater within the fortified city. A reservoir with an external feeding system was identified at Kadesh Barnea during the Iron Age II.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
