    <Placemark>
      <name>Khirbet Abu Tabaq (Kerem Atrad) (ח&apos;רבת אבו טבק (כרם עטרד))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Abu Tabaq (Kerem Atrad) (ח&apos;רבת אבו טבק (כרם עטרד))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Desert</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.30 (Pages 166, 167)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>The Abu Tabaq Cave, located at the foot of the fortress, served as a reservoir. It is 35m long, 7m wide, and 5m high, with a built entrance and steps leading inside. A rock-cut cistern, 18m from the Abu Tabaq Cave, approximately 6m deep with a 1m diameter opening. It is located beneath the fortress, suggesting a shaft for drawing water from within the fortification.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Khirbet Abu Tabaq (Kerem Atrad)</value></Data>
