    <Placemark>
      <name>Khirbet Bint-Barr (חורבת בנת בר)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Bint-Barr (חורבת בנת בר)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.21 (Pages 162, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Cisterns or pools were found at Bannat Bar, dated to the Iron Age II period. A rectangular plastered cistern (approx. 4x3m, 3.5m deep, 40 cubic meters) with Iron Age plaster, and two bell-shaped cisterns (one 3.5m diameter/depth, 23 cubic meters; another 6m diameter, 3m deep, 56 cubic meters) were identified, dating to the 8th century BCE.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Khirbet Bint-Barr</value></Data>
        <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>חורבת בנת בר</value></Data>
        <Data name="Era"><value>09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Plastered Cistern</value></Data>
        <Data name="Region"><value>Negev</value></Data>
        <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Dates"><value>-1000 to -586 BCE</value></Data>
        <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.9.21</value></Data>
        <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>162, 191</value></Data>
        <Data name="Description"><value>Cisterns or pools were found at Bannat Bar, dated to the Iron Age II period. A rectangular plastered cistern (approx. 4x3m, 3.5m deep, 40 cubic meters) with Iron Age plaster, and two bell-shaped cisterns (one 3.5m diameter/depth, 23 cubic meters; another 6m diameter, 3m deep, 56 cubic meters) were identified, dating to the 8th century BCE.</value></Data>
      </ExtendedData>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>35.05254,32.06171,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Khirbet Deir es-Sidd (חורבת דיר א-סיד)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Deir es-Sidd (חורבת דיר א-סיד)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.25 (Pages 164, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Rock-cut cisterns with channels leading to them were found on the steep slopes of this extensive settlement. These cisterns were used during the Iron Age II and continued into the Second Temple period. Cisterns or pools were found at Deir es-Sid, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
