      <name>Khirbet Marjameh (חורבת מרג&apos;מה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Marjameh (חורבת מרג&apos;מה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Samaria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.22 (Pages 162, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A rock-cut cistern opening was found near the 8th-century BCE fortifications, though its size and plaster type are unknown. The primary water source for the city was the large Ein Samia spring nearby. Cisterns or pools were found at Qala&apos; Marjama, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
