    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Azekah (תל עזקה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Azekah (תל עזקה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Ancient City Water System</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.50 (Pages 184)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>An Assyrian inscription (Azekah Inscription) from Sargon II&apos;s campaign (712 BCE) mentions &apos;water&apos; and &apos;canal&apos; in the context of conquering a city, possibly hinting at the use or destruction of a water system, or a siege tactic involving a water tunnel.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
