        <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>184</value></Data>
        <Data name="Description"><value>An Assyrian inscription (Azekah Inscription) from Sargon II&apos;s campaign (712 BCE) mentions &apos;water&apos; and &apos;canal&apos; in the context of conquering a city, possibly hinting at the use or destruction of a water system, or a siege tactic involving a water tunnel.</value></Data>
