    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Beit Mirsim (תל בית מרסים)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Beit Mirsim (תל בית מרסים)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.28 (Pages 165, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Several cisterns were found in Layer A (Iron Age II). One in the SE area (338-15) was 6m deep, with a built and rock-cut section, and a well-preserved, plastered channel leading to it from the NE, likely draining roofs. A settling basin was present at the channel&apos;s entry point. Cisterns or pools were found at Tel Beit Mirsim, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
