    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Halif (תל חליף)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Halif (תל חליף)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.32 (Pages 168, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A rectangular, well-plastered cistern, measuring 9x4x3.5m, was uncovered in Area IV. It is dated to the Iron Age II period. Cisterns or pools were found at Tel Halif, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
